          "rationale": "No non-compete or field-of-use restraint binds Customer anywhere in the Agreement. Searches for compete/competing/competitor, \"shall not\" prohibitions, exclusivity, sole-source and field-of-use/territory language returned no restraint on Bluefly's business. To the contrary, § 14.16 (Freedom of Action) expressly confirms that \"Each party is free to enter into similar agreements with others,\" so Customer remains free to buy or build competing hosting solutions. The only Customer-side prohibitions are licence-scope terms rather than restrictive covenants: § 14.11 bars reselling the Services, § 12.1 limits use of IBM's Base Components to use \"solely in connection with the Services\", and § 14.19 merely limits where IBM delivers. None of these restricts the businesses we may operate or the products we may buy or build, so the clause meets the preferred position and no redline is warranted.",
